.TH SUCKLESS-HARNESS 7 "September 2023" "suckless-harness 1.2"
.SH NAME
suckless-harness \- development setup and contribution guidelines
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBsuckless-harness\fR repository enforces suckless.org software engineering
principles. This document describes the environment setup and verification
process for contributing.
.SH PREREQUISITES
A C99 compiler (cc), awk, and GNU make.
.SH ENVIRONMENT SETUP
No external dependencies or runtime environments are required.
The primary artifact is \fBSKILL.md\fR.
.SH BUILD AND VERIFICATION
Run the test suite before submitting changes:
.PP
.RS
ASAN_OPTIONS=detect_leaks=0 sh test/run.sh
.RE
.PP
This extracts every C block from SKILL.md, compiles them, runs the
worked example, and executes syntax and memory checks.
.SH SUBMITTING CHANGES
Keep changes minimal, focused, and free of bloat. Ensure the test suite
passes. Submit changes via a pull request.
